---
import Prose from '../layouts/Prose.astro';
import { business, pricing, trailer } from '../config';
---

<Prose
  title={`Terms of Hire | ${business.name}`}
  heading="Terms of hire"
  description={`The terms for hiring the ${trailer.model} from ${business.name}.`}
  updated="11 November 2026"
>
  <p>These terms apply to every hire of the trailer from {business.name} ("we", "us"). By booking, you ("the hirer") agree to them.</p>

  <h2>1. Booking and payment</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>A booking is confirmed once we have agreed your dates. We will then send you the amount due and our bank details. There is no booking fee.</li>
    <li>Payment is by bank transfer only. The hire charge and the £{pricing.deposit} deposit must be received before you collect the trailer. Please use the payment reference we give you.</li>
    <li>
      Hire charges are: £{pricing.day} for one day, £{pricing.weekend} for a weekend (Saturday and Sunday), £{pricing.weekdays} for
      Monday to Friday, and £{pricing.extraDay} for each extra day. 
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2>2. Deposit</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>The £{pricing.deposit} deposit is returned by bank transfer when the trailer is returned on time on the agreed date.</li>
    <li>If the trailer is returned late, or with damage or missing equipment, we may keep some or all of the deposit to cover extra hire days, repairs or replacement.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>3. Your responsibilities</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>You must hold a full, valid driving licence that allows you to tow the trailer, and your vehicle must be legally able to tow its loaded weight.</li>
    <li>Your motor insurance must cover you for towing a trailer.</li>
    <li>
      Do not exceed the trailer’s maximum gross weight of {trailer.grossWeightKg.toLocaleString('en-GB')} kg (a load of about
      {' '}{trailer.payloadKg.toLocaleString('en-GB')} kg). Secure every load with the wheel straps supplied.
    </li>
    <li>Check the coupling, lights and tyres before every journey, and follow the Highway Code and towing speed limits.</li>
    <li>
      You are responsible for the trailer and its equipment (including the winch and wheel straps) from collection until return, and for any
      fines, penalties or charges incurred during the hire.
    </li>
    <li>Do not sub-hire or lend the trailer to anyone else.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>4. Faults and breakdowns</h2>
  <p>
    If the trailer develops a fault or is involved in an accident, stop when it is safe to do so and call us on
    <a href={business.phoneHref}>{business.phoneDisplay}</a>. Do not carry out repairs without our agreement.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Return</h2>
  <p>Return the trailer to the agreed place in {business.area}, at the agreed time, in the same condition you received it. Remove any debris from the deck.</p>

  <h2>6. Liability</h2>
  <p>
    We are not responsible for loss of or damage to any vehicle or goods carried on the trailer, except where caused by our negligence. Nothing in
    these terms limits liability that cannot be limited by law.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>Call <a href={business.phoneHref}>{business.phoneDisplay}</a> or email <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a>.</p>
</Prose>
